@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title Rating Systems — Selection Map (is version B stronger than A?)
' Synthesis: turning match outcomes into a comparable strength estimate with error bars
' Level:  1

actor "Human expert\npaired outcomes only" as H

component "Bradley-Terry\nlatent strength from pairings" as BT <<app>>
component "Elo\nincremental online update" as ELO <<app>>
component "Glicko\nstrength plus uncertainty" as GL <<host>>
database  "Rating with an interval\nnot a bare win rate" as R <<db>>

H ARROW_MAIN BT : batch of results,\nfit all players at once
H ARROW_OPTIONAL ELO : streaming updates,\none game at a time
H ARROW_MAIN GL : few games per player,\nuncertainty matters
BT ARROW_MAIN R
ELO ARROW_OPTIONAL R : point estimate only
GL ARROW_MAIN R : interval comes for free

note bottom of R
  **A win rate is not a verdict.** 55% over 40 games
  and 55% over 4000 games are different claims; only
  the second can gate a change. Report an interval,
  and pair seeds so colour and opening luck cancel.
  ----
  **Draws must be scored, not discarded.** In games
  with a turn cap, draws are common and dropping them
  biases the estimate. Note that plain Bradley-Terry
  has **no tie term**: scoring a draw as half a win is
  the Elo/Glicko convention, and modelling ties
  properly needs an extension (Rao-Kupper, Davidson)
  — see ""paired-comparison-rating.puml"".
  ----
  This is the measurement that licenses every other
  climb in this folder: without it, weight tuning
  optimizes an unmeasured guess (""../optimization/"").
end note
@enduml
